EEVEE: render on GPUs with 4 color attachments (no SSS), and never draw with a failed material

EEVEE Legacy's opaque material shader writes 6 color outputs (radiance, 2 for screen-space
reflections, 3 for Subsurface Scattering). V3D 4.2 (Raspberry Pi 4, Mesa v3d) has 4 color attachments,
so every lit material failed to link ("invalid explicit location 4 specified for 'sssRadius'") — the
default material and EEVEE's own pink error material too, as they use the same shader. EEVEE_material_get()
then returned the failed error material and the draw code made a shading group from its NULL shader:
F12 with EEVEE crashed (a segment violation; the BLI_assert that would catch it is off in release
builds).

- GPU_max_color_attachments() (GL: min(GL_MAX_COLOR_ATTACHMENTS, GL_MAX_DRAW_BUFFERS, 8)).
- eevee_legacy_material_surface_frag_opaque_no_sss: the opaque shader with 3 outputs, used when fewer
  than 6 attachments exist; the subsurface light is added to the radiance as for refraction.
- EFFECT_SSS stays off there, with a one-time message: subsurface materials render as diffuse.
- When not even the error material's shader compiles, EEVEE_material_get() returns NULL and the
  material is not drawn (depth and shadows only), instead of crashing.

docs/design/blender.md §2.2 (milestone M5).

